  "body": "**Final qualification passed at `b9213e327cc57733559033d84db605271fd8eb31`:** both complete local bases pass (5,411 passed, 70 skipped, 150 deselected each; 758.71/726.27 seconds), both optional suites pass (2,319 each; 485.50/423.26 seconds), and [both hosted jobs](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/actions/runs/44147362228) pass (5,411 each; 1093.67/1164.38 seconds). Strict typing covers 823 files; lint, formatting and hooks pass. The verifier checked actual Python 3.11.17/NumPy 2.4.6 and Python 3.12.15/NumPy 2.5.4 before and after local checks, all hosted uv selections, and equality of the entire tested checkout tree to this head. All 453 source hashes and numerical exports remain unchanged. The old failed optional cohort remains published and is not counted. The corrected regression checks parent refusal plus fresh-child isolation; all 31 focused tests also pass with OpenSpiel deliberately preloaded in the parent.\n\nIssue #4: the saved elapsed-stack profile puts most earlier-source loading time in the reader for an older training archive. This provides a better next code path to inspect than caching frozen opponents, without another profiling run.\n\nThe five functions were selected in the [preimplementation plan](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/issues/4#issuecomment-6954063964). Reader source [395575b](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/tree/395575bc2e3e94d4a89dbb5b799603908d16a944) was public before extraction. [Results, full tables and terminal commands](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/03c7022/docs/earlier-source-profile.md#historical-saved-data-result--november-17) retain all2,354frames and5,640edges, all five selected pages and every direct incoming/outgoing edge, with unmerged identities.\n\nAcross the historical profile's two earlier-source-loader calls, inclusive elapsed-stack time is138.044s. Its direct earlier-archive-loader edge is125.609s; the nested `reduced_study_run.read_saved` edge is125.552s. The loader's frozen-opponent edge is0.860610s/32calls, while16tiny-fixture calls belong to another caller. These are nested instrumented elapsed totals including waits, not current CPU costs or savings; they must not be added across levels. The largest child/self conservation residual is1.42109e-14s under the fixed1e-7s tolerance.\n\nBoth actual data readers (Python3.11.17/NumPy2.4.6 and3.12.15/2.5.4) reproduce all five numerical exports BYTEEXACT with104construction/profiling targets blocked, zero forbidden calls, all15raw producer files unchanged, and no new solver/profiler/training. [Actual receipts and export hashes](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/03c7022/results/earlier-source-profile/data-checks/manifest.json). Complete original source/pair/raw/scalar/replay/unit authentication, selected source hashes/AST coordinates, ambiguity/recursion rejection and output retention remain. The binary is hashed only. No missing/favorable selection or old gate waiver.\n\nAll31focused cases pass on both actual runtimes (0.93/0.92s), including a complete real saved-data regression with104guards and five exact output checks. Full strict typing823files, lint/format and519relative documentation links/affected anchors/markers pass. Source453 fingerprint60fd4402b14c429f94370f02dc65eaac7792f831f6ecca01e668ddbfb6d95b53 is unchanged between source and results commits; all450earlier scientific files remain byte-identical. The first complete cohort at03 passed bases/hosted base jobs but failed both optional suites on the shared-process guard; the full corrected-head cohort above must pass. The initial source-head draft CI is superseded, not counted as qualification; this milestone reads existing data and creates no new scientific producer/admission.\n\nThis coherent PR also [archives PR86's completed six-role/main checks](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/395575b/results/context-reuse/final-ci/manifest.json): retained initial hosted timeouts/local stalls, exact merge tree, main720tests/four exports/103guards and preservation of all ten user changes after checks. Its context-copy comparison stays REJECTED. Journal131/work log and three explanation questions distinguish elapsed/CPU, shared callers and unchanged strategy strength.\n\nSelf-review: all original identities/edges survive; direct edges avoid charging a shared callee's aggregate to a single caller. Existing output and changed raw inputs reject. No strategy, dependency, CI, compute cap, seed or research acceptance rule changes. Runtime912.54/900 and accuracy2.390%/1% still fail. Next inspect the earlier archive reader; no competitive/default/global/strength admission. Codex-assisted implementation/checks/drafting; no independent human review, personal practice or hours inferred.",
